  "method": "Real local listen server + initial remote, remote joining after damage/collapse, and third dense-snapshot late remote after complete wall removal. Four human slots. All remotes compare full HP/state digest, sampled actual UE collision every13 records and all native ISM mappings. The initial remote uses owned server weapon RPCs, walks through a replicated breach, and walks up/down two storeys with actual authoritative character movement. Three generation epochs then explosion state/collision parity. Eleven automated native tests separately check geometry and reversed/future/invalid snapshot transactions. No packaging/publication; no bandwidth/FPS/platform guarantee. Local simultaneous Unreal processes share CPU/GPU/memory. Incoming loss/lag is confirmed in each remote log. Network buffer counters describe owned arrays/maps only; actor/channel, shared/engine and GPU heaps are excluded. M4/M5 receipts are historical.",
